# M4 walkthrough: knowledge documents.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisites: the stack with SeaweedFS (pnpm stack:up, S3_ACCESS_KEY and S3_SECRET_KEY in .env),
# and a department with a specialist that has the knowledge_search tool (see m2-org.http).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here
@departmentId = paste-a-department-id

### Upload a document shared with every department (text, markdown, CSV, JSON, HTML or PDF, up to 20 MiB)
# @name shared
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/knowledge
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=superagent

--superagent
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Retention policy
--superagent
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="retention.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

# Data retention

Customer records are kept for ninety days, then deleted.
--superagent--

### Upload one only a department searches
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/knowledge
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=superagent

--superagent
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="departmentId"

{{departmentId}}
--superagent
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="discounts.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Discount rules: never exceed fifteen percent.
--superagent--

### Search like an agent of that department would (its documents and the shared ones)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/knowledge/search?q=how long are customer records kept&departmentId={{departmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### All documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/knowledge
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete one (the file and its passages)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/knowledge/{{shared.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
